<h2>A major basmati market, despite the logistics environment</h2>
<p>Yemen is, by the trade data we've verified, one of the largest single-country markets for Indian basmati rice anywhere in the world — reflecting rice's role as a dietary staple and long-standing trade ties between Indian exporters and Yemeni importers that have persisted through a difficult operating environment.</p>

<p>We won't pretend the logistics picture is as simple as it is for, say, a Gulf market with stable port infrastructure. Yemen's ports and inland transport have been affected by prolonged conflict, and specific routing, port availability, and realistic transit windows are things we confirm at the time of your order rather than assume from general shipping-line schedules.</p>

<h2>Payment structured to the situation</h2>
<p>Given the banking and logistics environment, we don't default to open account or assume standard LC terms will move smoothly. Payment structure — confirmed letter of credit, advance payment, or a combination — is agreed with each buyer before booking, based on the specific route and counterpart bank involved.</p>

